WEBVTT

00:00.500 --> 00:05.870
A factor is a number that multiplies with another number to make a product.

00:05.870 --> 00:08.232
Let's find the factors of twelve.

00:08.682 --> 00:16.554
Twelve counters can make a row of twelve. One times twelve is twelve. So one and twelve are factors.

00:17.004 --> 00:24.039
They can make two rows of six. Two times six is twelve. So two and six are factors.

00:24.489 --> 00:31.734
They can make three rows of four. Three times four is twelve. So three and four are factors.

00:32.184 --> 00:37.269
The factors of twelve are one, two, three, four, six and twelve.

00:37.719 --> 00:45.067
Multiples go the other way. They are the numbers in a times table. The multiples of four are four,

00:45.067 --> 00:47.541
eight, twelve, sixteen and so on.
